  children:
  - seconds: 124
    speaker: Eliot Wertheimer
    text: Good evening everybody. I hope the beginning of everyone's school year has
      gone well. School started at all seven schools, and I was amazed to see just
      how smoothly things ran on the first day, with buses, prepared lessons, cleaned
      schools, and nutritional staff all contributing. At the high school, class meetings,
      photos, and resource introductions took place, while middle schoolers had orientation
      activities and showed good compliance with phone policies. Kaler Elementary
      School added 41 kindergarten students, leading to the process of adding a third
      kindergarten classroom, and Skillin Elementary School welcomed 56 kindergartners,
      with students quickly living up to school expectations. Athletic teams have
      moved into the regular season with several wins, and the all-staff convocation
      on August 27th highlighted the superintendent's speech on acts of hope and love,
      which resonated with the strength shown by students after news of another school
      shooting.
